[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625454447","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625454447","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625454447,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cfUFv","user":{"login":"yliu120","id":9438093,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MzgwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9438093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120","html_url":"https://github.com/yliu120","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T20:00:51Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T20:00:51Z","body":"@hawkinsp ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625454447/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625461289","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625461289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625461289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cfVwp","user":{"login":"yliu120","id":9438093,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MzgwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9438093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120","html_url":"https://github.com/yliu120","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T20:04:10Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T20:04:10Z","body":"In addition to this bug,\n\nif there is an API that explicitly controls the lifetime of the np array created from jax.array, can you please the np. array also writable?\nThis is a natural request as if the users have control over the lifetime, then they can make sure writing to the buffer can be done before the next execute call.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625461289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625559813","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625559813","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625559813,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cft0F","user":{"login":"heiner","id":69371,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5Mzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69371?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner","html_url":"https://github.com/heiner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T20:52:41Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T20:56:30Z","body":"Interestingly, this repro works for `float16` but shows the same issue for `bfloat16`:\n\n```py\nimport jax\nimport numpy as np\nfrom jax import numpy as jnp\n\n\ndef main():\n    d_tensor = jnp.array(0, dtype=jnp.bfloat16)\n\n    d_sharding = d_tensor.sharding\n    h_sharding = d_sharding.with_memory_kind(\"pinned_host\")\n\n    h_tensor = jax.device_put(d_tensor, h_sharding)\n\n    def d2h_copy(src, dst):\n        dst = jax.device_put(src, h_sharding)\n        return src, dst\n\n    d2h_copy_jit = jax.jit(\n        d2h_copy,\n        in_shardings=(h_sharding, d_sharding),\n        out_shardings=(h_sharding, d_sharding),\n        donate_argnums=(0, 1),\n        keep_unused=True,\n    )\n\n    np.array(h_tensor)\n\n    # This line fixes it (or not using bfloat16 above).\n    # h_tensor._npy_value = np.array(-1, dtype=h_tensor.dtype)\n\n    h_tensor, d_tensor = d2h_copy_jit(h_tensor, d_tensor)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625559813/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625591160","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625591160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625591160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cf1d4","user":{"login":"heiner","id":69371,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5Mzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69371?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner","html_url":"https://github.com/heiner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T21:04:13Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T21:46:14Z","body":"I believe if it raises here, the refcounts are off somehow: https://cs.opensource.google/tensorflow/tensorflow/+/master:third_party/xla/xla/python/py_array.cc;l=1530\n\nSo the `__array__` codepath causes trouble when donating.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625591160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625669570","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625669570","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625669570,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cgInC","user":{"login":"jakevdp","id":781659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T21:49:44Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T21:51:07Z","body":"> can you please the np. array also writable?\n\nThis will not be possible in general. JAX arrays are immutable, and conversion to NumPy is done in a zero-copy manner whenever possible. Thus the resulting NumPy arrays will also be read-only: if you want to write into the buffer, you'll need to make a copy.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625669570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625672203","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625672203","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625672203,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cgJQL","user":{"login":"jakevdp","id":781659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T21:51:21Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T21:51:53Z","body":"> So the `__array__` codepath causes trouble when donating.\n\nThanks for this insight! I think it's definitely possible that there's some fishy behavior around donation and cacheing of the host-side array.\n\nAssigning @dfm, but Dan feel free to bump to someone else if needed.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625672203/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625680318","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625680318","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625680318,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cgLO-","user":{"login":"heiner","id":69371,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5Mzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69371?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner","html_url":"https://github.com/heiner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heiner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T21:56:21Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T21:56:21Z","body":"> This will not be possible in general. JAX arrays are immutable, and conversion to NumPy is done in a zero-copy manner whenever possible. Thus the resulting NumPy arrays will also be read-only: if you want to write into the buffer, you'll need to make a copy.\n\nIt is technically possible, I can for instance do\n\n```py\n__array_interface__ = np.array(jax_array, copy=False).__array_interface__\nptr, _ = __array_interface__[\"data\"]\n__array_interface__[\"data\"] = (ptr, False)\n```\n\nand then give `__array_interface__` back to Numpy.\n\nIt would be better if JAX gave me a way to not require that hack though. Why would I want to do this? For instance in order to write into the pinned host memory at checkpoint loading time (for instance, using `ts.array(a).write(ts_data)`). It would be better if JAX had a less hacky way to do this, as without that pinned host memory is far less useful.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625680318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625702946","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625702946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625702946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cgQwi","user":{"login":"jakevdp","id":781659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T22:10:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T22:11:17Z","body":"> It is technically possible, I can for instance do\n\nI mean, sure. It's Python, you can do whatever you want. What I'm saying is that we **deliberately** make the buffer read-only because to do otherwise would lead to bugs, because the JAX runtime assumes the buffers that back its arrays are immutable. I would not suggest using code that works around that in any important context.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625702946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625704678","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625704678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625704678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cgRLm","user":{"login":"yliu120","id":9438093,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MzgwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9438093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120","html_url":"https://github.com/yliu120","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T22:11:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T22:11:28Z","body":"> > can you please the np. array also writable?\n> \n> This will not be possible in general. JAX arrays are immutable, and conversion to NumPy is done in a zero-copy manner whenever possible. Thus the resulting NumPy arrays will also be read-only: if you want to write into the buffer, you'll need to make a copy.\n\nactually making array mutable is not a bad idea in case of saving large copies.\nand jax does have some mutable array proposals. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625704678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625707081","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2625707081","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2625707081,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6cgRxJ","user":{"login":"yliu120","id":9438093,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MzgwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9438093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120","html_url":"https://github.com/yliu120","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T22:13:05Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T22:13:05Z","body":"> > So the `__array__` codepath causes trouble when donating.\n> \n> Thanks for this insight! I think it's definitely possible that there's some fishy behavior around donation and cacheing of the host-side array.\n> \n> Assigning [@dfm](https://github.com/dfm), but Dan feel free to bump to someone else if needed.\n\nIf a buffer is OnCpu, then it is created with ZeroCopy code path. Then the created ndarray is basically something not too different from a shared_ptr. In that case, there is no need to cache.\nI think the fix should include this consideration.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2625707081/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2642781651","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2642781651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2642781651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6dhaXT","user":{"login":"jaro-sevcik","id":17763629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYzNjI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17763629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik","html_url":"https://github.com/jaro-sevcik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaro-sevcik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T12:23:56Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T12:24:49Z","body":"@dfm , @yashk2810 \n\nHow palatable would be to only cache `_npy_value` if it requires a copy?\n\nI am imagining something like:\n```python\ndiff --git a/jax/_src/array.py b/jax/_src/array.py\nindex 802a3f5f6..6fb07abc4 100644\n--- a/jax/_src/array.py\n+++ b/jax/_src/array.py\n@@ -603,6 +603,13 @@ class ArrayImpl(basearray.Array):\n   def _single_device_array_to_np_array(self):\n     return np.asarray(self._arrays[0])\n\n+  def _single_device_array_as_np_array_did_copy(self):\n+    npy_value = self._single_device_array_to_np_array()\n+    # This is a hack, ideally _single_device_array_to_np_array\n+    # would return the `did_copy` bool from the C++ implementation.\n+    did_copy = npy_value.ctypes.data != self._arrays[0].unsafe_buffer_pointer()\n+    return npy_value, did_copy\n+\n   @use_cpp_method()\n   def _copy_single_device_array_to_host_async(self):\n     self._arrays[0].copy_to_host_async()\n@@ -624,9 +631,11 @@ class ArrayImpl(basearray.Array):\n\n     if self._npy_value is None:\n       if self.is_fully_replicated:\n-        self._npy_value = self._single_device_array_to_np_array()\n-        self._npy_value.flags.writeable = False\n-        return cast(np.ndarray, self._npy_value)\n+        npy_value, did_copy = self._single_device_array_as_np_array_did_copy()\n+        npy_value.flags.writeable = False\n+        if did_copy:\n+          self._npy_value = npy_value\n+        return cast(np.ndarray, npy_value)\n\n       # TODO(yashkatariya): Merge `_process_has_full_value_in_mcjax` with\n       # is_fully_addressable.\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2642781651/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2657355511","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2657355511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2657355511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6eZAb3","user":{"login":"dfm","id":350282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MDI4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/350282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm","html_url":"https://github.com/dfm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-13T17:59:47Z","updated_at":"2025-02-13T17:59:47Z","body":"I fixed this specific behavior in https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/pull/26460 and https://github.com/openxla/xla/pull/22586 by updating the caching logic for zero copy device arrays. I did it just like @jaro-sevcik suggested (the less hacky version :D).\n\nThere's a more general point that there should be a better mechanism for clearing this cache, or otherwise being more explicit about copies, but I'll leave that for future work!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2657355511/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2657933345","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216#issuecomment-2657933345","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/26216","id":2657933345,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6ebNgh","user":{"login":"yliu120","id":9438093,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MzgwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9438093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120","html_url":"https://github.com/yliu120","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-13T23:39:56Z","updated_at":"2025-02-13T23:45:13Z","body":"\n>> There's a more general point that there should be a better mechanism for clearing this cache, or otherwise being more explicit about copies, but I'll leave that for future work!\n\nI think this would be better as well. \n\nAnother point is that whether this value is cached or not is a user decision. It is probably better to leave the cache mechanism completely to users so that they don't have to reason about the lifetime of the _npy_value ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/2657933345/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]